Building an online forum using the **LAMP stack** (Linux, Apache, MySQL, PHP) is a classic web development project. 

Below is a complete, step-by-step tutorial for building a functional, lightweight forum from scratch.

---

### Prerequisites
1. **A LAMP environment installed on your machine.**
   * **Linux:** Local Ubuntu/Debian server.
   * **Windows alternative:** XAMPP or WampServer.
   * **Mac alternative:** MAMP.
2. **Basic understanding** of HTML, PHP, and SQL.

---

### Step 1: Design the Database (MySQL)

A basic forum needs three main tables: **Users**, **Topics** (or Threads), and **Replies** (or Posts).

Open **phpMyAdmin** or your MySQL command line, create a database named `lamp_forum`, and run this SQL script:

```sql
CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS lamp_forum;
USE lamp_forum;

-- 1. Users Table
CREATE TABLE users (
    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    username VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    email VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    password VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 2. Topics Table
CREATE TABLE topics (
    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    title VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    user_id INT NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
);

-- 3. Replies Table
CREATE TABLE replies (
    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    topic_id INT NOT NULL,
    user_id INT NOT NULL,
    content TEXT NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    FOREIGN KEY (topic_id) REFERENCES topics(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
);
```

---

### Step 2: Set Up Directory & Database Connection

Create a folder in your server's web root (e.g., `/var/www/html/forum` or `htdocs/forum`).

Create a file named `db.php` to handle the MySQL connection via **PDO** (PHP Data Objects), which helps prevent SQL injection.

**`db.php`**
```php
<?php
$host = 'localhost';
$dbname = 'lamp_forum';
$username = 'root'; // Change if needed
$password = '';     // Change if needed

try {
    $pdo = new PDO("mysql:host=$host;dbname=$dbname;charset=utf8mb4", $username, $password);
    $pdo->setAttribute(PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE, PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION);
    $pdo->setAttribute(PDO::ATTR_DEFAULT_FETCH_MODE, PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);
} catch (PDOException $e) {
    die("Database connection failed: " . $e->getMessage());
}
?>
```

---

### Step 3: Create User Registration & Login System

Users need to log in to post topics or replies.

#### **`register.php`**
```php
<?php
require 'db.php';
$message = '';

if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] == 'POST') {
    $username = trim($_POST['username']);
    $email    = trim($_POST['email']);
    $password = password_hash($_POST['password'], PASSWORD_DEFAULT); // Secure password hashing

    $stmt = $pdo->prepare("INSERT INTO users (username, email, password) VALUES (?, ?, ?)");
    try {
        $stmt->execute([$username, $email, $password]);
        header("Location: login.php");
        exit;
    } catch (PDOException $e) {
        $message = "Username or Email already exists.";
    }
}
?>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><title>Register</title></head>
<body>
    <h2>Register</h2>
    <p><?= $message ?></p>
    <form method="POST">
        <input type="text" name="username" placeholder="Username" required><br><br>
        <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Email" required><br><br>
        <input type="password" name="password" placeholder="Password" required><br><br>
        <button type="submit">Register</button>
    </form>
    <p>Already have an account? <a href="login.php">Login here</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
```

#### **`login.php`**
```php
<?php
session_start();
require 'db.php';
$message = '';

if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] == 'POST') {
    $username = trim($_POST['username']);
    $password = $_POST['password'];

    $stmt = $pdo->prepare("SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?");
    $stmt->execute([$username]);
    $user = $stmt->fetch();

    if ($user && password_verify($password, $user['password'])) {
        // Log the user in via Session
        $_SESSION['user_id'] = $user['id'];
        $_SESSION['username'] = $user['username'];
        header("Location: index.php");
        exit;
    } else {
        $message = "Invalid username or password.";
    }
}
?>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><title>Login</title></head>
<body>
    <h2>Login</h2>
    <p><?= $message ?></p>
    <form method="POST">
        <input type="text" name="username" placeholder="Username" required><br><br>
        <input type="password" name="password" placeholder="Password" required><br><br>
        <button type="submit">Login</button>
    </form>
    <p>Need an account? <a href="register.php">Register here</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
```

#### **`logout.php`**
```php
<?php
session_start();
session_destroy();
header("Location: index.php");
exit;
?>
```

---

### Step 4: Homepage & Topic Creation

The homepage displays all forum topics and allows logged-in users to create a new thread.

#### **`index.php`**
```php
<?php
session_start();
require 'db.php';

// Fetch all topics with author usernames
$sql = "SELECT topics.*, users.username 
        FROM topics 
        JOIN users ON topics.user_id = users.id 
        ORDER BY topics.created_at DESC";
$stmt = $pdo->query($sql);
$topics = $stmt->fetchAll();
?>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><title>LAMP Forum</title></head>
<body>
    <h1>Forum Home</h1>

    <?php if (isset($_SESSION['user_id'])): ?>
        <p>Welcome, <strong><?= htmlspecialchars($_SESSION['username']) ?></strong>! | <a href="logout.php">Logout</a></p>
        <a href="create_topic.php"><strong>+ Create New Topic</strong></a>
    <?php else: ?>
        <p><a href="login.php">Login</a> or <a href="register.php">Register</a> to post.</p>
    <?php endif; ?>

    <hr>

    <h3>Topics</h3>
    <ul>
        <?php foreach ($topics as $topic): ?>
            <li>
                <a href="topic.php?id=<?= $topic['id'] ?>">
                    <?= htmlspecialchars($topic['title']) ?>
                </a> 
                <em>by <?= htmlspecialchars($topic['username']) ?> on <?= $topic['created_at'] ?></em>
            </li>
        <?php endforeach; ?>
    </ul>
</body>
</html>
```

#### **`create_topic.php`**
```php
<?php
session_start();
require 'db.php';

if (!isset($_SESSION['user_id'])) {
    header("Location: login.php");
    exit;
}

if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] == 'POST') {
    $title = trim($_POST['title']);
    $user_id = $_SESSION['user_id'];

    if (!empty($title)) {
        $stmt = $pdo->prepare("INSERT INTO topics (title, user_id) VALUES (?, ?)");
        $stmt->execute([$title, $user_id]);

        $topic_id = $pdo->lastInsertId();
        header("Location: topic.php?id=" . $topic_id);
        exit;
    }
}
?>
